From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: patrickjquinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 18:28:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: mediatek: mt8781-zinwa-q25: Set the proximity
 near level

The node carries the vendor firmware's near threshold of 3800, which
belongs to that firmware's own baseline-tracking proximity algorithm.
With the hx32062se driver the raw count reads 0 with nothing near the
phone and about 1400 with a finger over the sensor window, so 3800 is
never reached and nothing is ever reported as near.

Use 600, which separates the two through the Q25's cover glass.

Signed-off-by: patrickjquinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt8781-zinwa-q25.dts | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt8781-zinwa-q25.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt8781-zinwa-q25.dts
index 2886f9d7..a61df551 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt8781-zinwa-q25.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt8781-zinwa-q25.dts
@@ -884,7 +884,7 @@
 	light-sensor@2b {
 		compatible = "tyhx,hx32062se";
 		reg = <0x2b>;
-		proximity-near-level = <3800>;
+		proximity-near-level = <600>;
 	};
 };
 
